    "specPath": "specs/042-decision-service-and-remote-seams/spec.md",
    "status": "approved",
    "summary": "An amendment of approved spec 010 (R-16), for #76 child A2 (#57). Makes the `rustev-serve` service API concrete as `rustev.serve/1`: plan registration by content identity from plain or signed plan bundles, decisions, cancellation, lookup, server-sent event streaming, offline replay, evaluation and explanation, health, readiness and OpenMetrics, served over HTTP/1.1 and HTTP/2 with JSON and over gRPC from one handler layer, on TCP and Unix domain socket listeners. Defines two new transport-neutral callback protocols with an HTTP binding, `rustev.remote-context/1` (describe, fetch, acquire, cancel and invalidation by push or poll) and `rustev.remote-sink/1` (describe and deliver with receipts), behind bounded queues with deadlines, cancellation and typed refusals when full. Adds no plan construct: every `PlanId`, run record and judgment byte is unchanged. Approved (A-39) under the 2026-10-16 delivery work order; implementation is pending, and `rustev-serve` implementation still waits for the owner's approval of its spec 010 section 3.4 binding record (R-34 in the founding decisions).\n",
    "title": "Decision service sidecar and remote context and sink protocols (amends 010)"
